// Phase 10 Plan 07 -- QLT-04's declared composition depth 3, ACCEPTING
// member. Chain of 4 functions (leaf, f2, f1, caller), the shape the
// definition adopted from corevalidate_peer_liveness.go:64-77 calls "a
// chain of d+1 functions" (D-10-45), and every OpCall in the chain
// composes (f2 calls leaf, f1 calls f2, caller calls f1).
//
// FINDING (empirically confirmed, reported per this task's own escape
// hatch): the IDEAL depth-3 accept shape -- a SINGLE loan declared via
// `-> borrow(buffer) Buffer` at every hop, forwarded leaf-to-f2-to-f1-to-
// caller exactly like relay_depth2_refuse.lang's own middle hop, but with
// no conflicting `take` so the full CLI would admit it -- does NOT exist
// in this compiler today. `check.Program` alone admits that shape with
// ZERO diagnostics (verified: `go run ./cmd/dbgcheck` against the shape
// prints `check diagnostics=[]`), but `corevalidate.Validate` -- consulted
// next in `session.CheckCommandFile`'s fixed precedence -- independently
// REFUSES it with `core.callee_not_callable`, because
// `corevalidate.go`'s `peerDeriveOriginFacts` (the peer's own origin
// re-derivation `peerCallable` consults) has NO `core.OpCall` case at all:
// its forward walk only ever extends `derived[...]` through
// `OpBorrowShared`/`OpBorrowExclusive`/`OpMove`/`OpCopy`, so a middle
// function whose declared borrow return is sourced from FORWARDING A
// CALL'S RESULT is unconditionally judged "not derived" and therefore not
// Callable -- regardless of what the callee (leaf) actually does, and
// regardless of whether the caller has any conflicting use at all. This
// affects `relay_depth2_refuse.lang` too (confirmed directly: with its own
// `take buffer` conflict removed, `corevalidate.Validate` still refuses
// `relay` as not-callable) -- it has simply never been OBSERVABLE there,
// because `check`'s own `check.interprocedural_loan_liveness` refusal
// already fires first and CheckCommandFile's fixed check-then-peer
// precedence never reaches corevalidate for that fixture. This is a
// genuine, previously-undocumented gap in corevalidate's origin peer,
// structurally analogous to D-10-28 (a second detector missing an OpCall
// case) but for the ORIGIN peer rather than the usesParam peer -- named
// here, not fixed, since `corevalidate.go` is outside this plan's
// `files_modified` and fixing it is exactly the kind of unscoped semantic
// change D-10-29 already declined once for a sibling peer. Also
// structurally impossible to route AROUND within one function: passing a
// borrow into a call consumes it (`ownership.use_after_move` fires the
// instant a borrowed place is both passed to a callee and returned
// afterward), so there is no expressible way to both forward a borrow
// through a call and ALSO independently re-derive it from the parameter
// directly.
//
// NEAREST EXPRESSIBLE SHAPE (this fixture): f2, a MIDDLE hop, creates a
// genuine local borrow of its own parameter (`borrowed`), forwards it into
// a real call to leaf (exercising pathoracle's own per-path composition
// machinery, `hasOpCall`/`composeLinearizeCaller`/`composeCall`, on a path
// that genuinely crosses an OpCall), and then -- once that borrow's last
// use is the leaf call -- takes ownership of its own parameter and returns
// it OWNED. The overall call chain still reaches the declared depth-3
// shape (4 functions, 3 OpCall hops: caller->f1->f2->leaf), and a genuine
// borrow (not a bare owned pass-through, unlike relay_depth2_accept.lang)
// is created, used across a call boundary, and released -- but the LOAN
// ITSELF crosses only 1 hop (f2->leaf), not all 3, because a 3-hop
// DECLARED-ORIGIN carry is exactly the shape corevalidate's above defect
// makes unrepresentable as an accepting program today. The genuine
// 3-hop declared-borrow carry IS exercised, structurally, by this
// fixture's twin, relay_depth3_refuse.lang: its checked core.Program
// (produced regardless of check's own refusal) is what
// TestCompositionDepthCorpusReachesDeclaredBound's corpus walk uses to
// observe the declared depth actually being reached, since pathoracle's
// own structural analysis is check/corevalidate-verdict-agnostic by
// design (pathoracle.go's own package doc).
//
// Expected, verified empirically via `go run ./cmd/lang --json check`:
// exit 0, status "valid" (previously named "pass" in this CLI's own
// vocabulary), empty diagnostics array. QLT-04.

module phase10.relay_depth3_accept

export {
  fn caller
}

fn leaf(buffer: Buffer) -> borrow(buffer) Buffer {
  let observed = borrow buffer
  observed
}

fn f2(buffer: Buffer) -> Buffer {
  let borrowed = borrow buffer
  let observed = leaf(borrowed)
  let taken = take buffer
  taken
}

fn f1(buffer: Buffer) -> Buffer {
  let forwarded = f2(buffer)
  forwarded
}

fn caller(buffer: Buffer) -> Buffer {
  let aliased = f1(buffer)
  aliased
}
